---
const TX = { from: 'wallet-a', to: 'merchant-7', amount: 120 };
---
<div class="demo" data-sign>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><button type="button" data-act="key" disabled>1 · Make a key on this device</button> <span class="fp" data-fp></span></li>
    <li><button type="button" data-act="sign" disabled>2 · Sign the payment</button></li>
    <li><label><input type="checkbox" data-tamper disabled /> Change the amount on the way to the gateway</label></li>
    <li><button type="button" data-act="send" disabled>3 · Send it to the gateway</button></li>
  </ol>
  <pre class="tx" data-tx>{JSON.stringify(TX)}</pre>
  <div class="log" data-log role="log" aria-label="What the gateway saw" tabindex="0">
    <p>// the gateway only ever receives the payment, the signature and the public key</p>
  </div>
  <p class="nojs" data-nojs>
    This demo needs JavaScript. It makes a P-256 (secp256r1) key pair in your browser that can't be exported, signs a toy payment
    with it, and lets a pretend gateway check the signature with the public key alone. Changing the amount after signing makes the
    check fail.
  </p>
</div>

<script>
  import '../scripts/lab-sign';
</script>

<style>
  .demo {
    margin-top: 24px; padding: clamp(18px, 4vw, 30px); border-radius: 18px; border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12);
    background: linear-gradient(150deg, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.06), rgb(255 255 255 / 0.01) 40%, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.03)), rgb(13 13 17 / 0.72);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.14), 0 30px 60px -30px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.9);
    backdrop-filter: blur(14px) saturate(1.4);
    display: grid; gap: 14px;
  }
  .steps { list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .steps li { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; align-items: center; }
  button {
    min-height: 46px; padding: 10px 16px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12); background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.04); color: var(--ink);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.08); font: 500 15px var(--font-display); cursor: pointer; transition: border-color 0.2s, background-color 0.2s;
  }
  button:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.28); background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.07); }
  button:disabled { cursor: not-allowed; color: var(--muted); border-style: dashed; background: transparent; box-shadow: none; }
  input:disabled { cursor: not-allowed; }
  label { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; color: var(--ink-2); cursor: pointer; }
  input { width: 18px; height: 18px; accent-color: var(--accent); }
  .fp { font: 500 13px var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .tx { font: 400 13.5px var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent-hi); background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px 14px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .log {
    font: 400 13.5px/1.7 var(--font-mono); color: var(--muted); background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px; min-height: 140px; max-height: 300px; overflow-y: auto; overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .log :global(p + p) { margin-top: 6px; }
  .log :global(.tone-ok) { color: var(--ok); }
  .log :global(.tone-bad) { color: var(--bad); }
  .nojs { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
</style>
